It is Saturday morning, and I am drinking coffee in my living room.
Suddenly, there is a knock on the door.
It is my neighbour, Nina.
She smiles and comes in.
"It is cold but clear today," she says.
"You should go out and see the city."
I ask her what I should see.
"Go down to the harbour," Nina answers.
"The old streets are very beautiful."
I do not know the way, so she helps me.
"Take bus number forty-two," she says.
"And get off at the big square."
I thank her for the good recommendation.
I put on my jacket and find my keys.
I am ready to explore the city.
